2026-09-23T07:08:15.7653631Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7653802Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654027Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654105Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654206Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654280Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654380Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654459Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654559Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654651Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654743Z             return x + 1
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654817Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654896Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7654987Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7655081Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7655155Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7655235Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7655324Z     To execute it::
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7655398Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7655483Z         $ pytest
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7655651Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7655738Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7655817Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7655913Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7655997Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7656139Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7656308Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7656393Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7656483Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7656577Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7656669Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7656764Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7656838Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7656948Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7657101Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7657176Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7657342Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7658102Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7658181Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7658256Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7658339Z     Features
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7658426Z     --------
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7658500Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7659177Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7659262Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7659351Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7659648Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7659750Z       of test modules and functions
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7659829Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7660096Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7660268Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7660350Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7660611Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7660722Z       test suites out of the box
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7660805Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7660906Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7660982Z     
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7661476Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
2026-09-23T07:08:15.7661556Z     
